From 5fd2dc59cd04e6639a31bcd7f4862d8186a05b16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:27:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Profiling sections declared as ranges of roctx (option
 enable-roctx)

On a GPU, the time table of the profiling gives the time of each section,
not what the GPU does during it. With the CMake option `enable-roctx` (OFF
by default, MFEM being compiled with HIP), `mfem_mgis::initialize` sets the
markers of the profiling sections of MGIS (`mgis::setProfilingMarkers`)
when it creates a device using a GPU, next to their synchronization: each
active section is declared as a range of roctx, the annotation library of
ROCm, which its profilers (rocprofv3) show with the calls of the HIP
runtime, the kernels and the memory copies. Nothing changes in the sources
which declare the sections. Without the option, roctx is neither searched
nor used, and no code is compiled.

Module `FindROCTX.cmake`: roctx of rocprofiler-sdk, else the one of
roctracer, which has the same functions.

Test `ProfilingMarkersTest`: markers set with the option and a GPU, and
only then, same profiling tree with or without them, ranges read in the
trace of rocprofv3 when it is found next to roctx. Documentation.
